{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Like a snail:</b> In the words of the ancients, of blessed memory: 'He created the snail,' and it is like the form of a fish in water that dissolves as it walks. And some say that the lamed of שבלול is doubled, and it is like שבולת מים (wave of water); this too is correct. And now I shall state the grammatical analysis of אשת. Know that the heh is a sign of the feminine, עטרה and תפארה, and when they exchange the heh for a tav, the word becomes milra, whether the word is in construct state, like תפארת ישראל, or not in construct state, and likewise עטרת and תפארת. So too אשת: at first אשה, and afterwards אשת, whether in construct state, like אשת איש, or not in construct state, like אשת יפת תואר."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {0 "The ancients' citation appears to reference a midrashic tradition; rendered literally as received."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:11.970063365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}